-- title:
--   Finite flat prolongation of a Hopf-realised subgroup of J₀(N₀p)[p]
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $N_0$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N_0$ and $p \neq 2$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $p$ in the sense that $p$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData` for $(N_0,p,A)$ satisfying `IsJacobian` (its structure morphism is an abelian scheme over $\mathbb Z_{(p)} =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), its relative group law is commutative and compatible with the parametrisations of $J_0(N_0)$-points, Galois-equivariant, compatible with reduction when the mod-$\ell$ reduction inputs hold, and Hecke-equivariant), let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP` for these data and $F$ a `NeronExtension` of $O$, so that $F$ provides a scheme `F.Nfull` over `shBase A` $=\operatorname{Spec}$ of the valuation ring of $A$ in the inertia-fixed field, with commutative group law satisfying the Néron model property bundle, an open immersion from the base change of $O.g$, a specialisation map onto the component group, and the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points `F.ptsN x` attached to $x \in J_0(N_0p)$. Assume: for every $m$ coprime to $p$, every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ and every $m$-torsion $x$, the displacement $\sigma\cdot x - x$ lies in `O.toricPts m`, the subgroup generated by the toric points; and for every $m>0$ the same displacements lie in `O.finPts m`, the subgroup generated by the $m$-torsion points extending to $A$-points. Let $V$ be an additive subgroup of $J_0(N_0p)$ contained in the $p$-torsion, and let $H$ be a commutative ring carrying a cocommutative Hopf algebra structure over $\mathbb Z_{(p)}$ that is finite and flat as a module, together with a bijection $e$ from the $\mathbb Z_{(p)}$-algebra homomorphisms $H \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ under the convolution product onto $V$ which is additive, $e(f*g) = e(f)+e(g)$, and Galois-compatible: whenever $g = \sigma \circ f$ pointwise for $\sigma \in \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$, one has $e(g) = \sigma \cdot e(f)$ in $J_0(N_0p)$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a scheme $X$, a morphism $g_X : X \to$ `shBase A` and a morphism $\varphi : X \to$ `F.Nfull` with $\varphi$ followed by `F.gN` equal to $g_X$, such that $g_X$ is finite and flat, every $v \in V$ admits a point $x$ of $X$ over the composite $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `shBase A` with $x$ followed by $\varphi$ equal to `F.ptsN v`, and conversely every such point $x$ of $X$ arises this way from some $v \in V$.
--
--   This is the Raynaud-style prolongation step: a subgroup $V$ of $J_0(N_0p)[p]$ realised as the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points of a finite flat commutative cocommutative Hopf algebra over $\mathbb Z_{(p)}$ is spread out over the base of the Néron extension, its points being exactly the images of the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-points of a finite flat scheme mapping to the Néron model. The statement is weaker than the classical one in that $\varphi$ is only required to be a morphism over the base, not a closed immersion; it is used by [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.NeronExtension.extN_of_mem_of_hopf_of_forall_smul_sub_mem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.NeronExtension.extN_of_mem_of_hopf_of_forall_smul_sub_mem) to show that the points of $V$ extend over the base.
